# This directory holds OPTIONAL extra Caddy sites, imported by the main Caddyfile.
#
# It exists because the office network blocks outbound port 22, so an SSH tunnel — the usual way to
# reach a staging container bound to 127.0.0.1 — cannot be opened from a laptop here. Anything that
# has to be LOOKED at rather than curl'd must therefore arrive over HTTPS on 443, like the portal
# itself.
#
# This file is a deliberate no-op. It only guarantees the import glob in ../Caddyfile always matches
# at least one file, so a fresh clone with no extra sites still starts. Adding or removing a real
# site here changes NOTHING about production until Caddy is reloaded.
#
# To publish staging, copy the template and fill in the two blanks:
#     cp caddy.d/staging.caddy.example caddy.d/staging.caddy
# then edit it and run:
#     docker exec humiley_caddy caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#
# To take it down again, delete the file and reload. Full instructions: docs/STAGING.md.
